**Theorem 7.4 (codec-transfer and cycle laws).** For every
$h\in\mathcal Z_\circ$ with its corresponding actually acquired binding
$b$, each independent decoder terminates on its authentic body and returns
exactly $h,W(h)$. Each direct arrow terminates and yields
the next independently defined view of the identical $h$. The composite
returns the identical initial S-body. On each accepted canonical image
re-encoding after decoding is the identity. S/B raw shape inverses also
hold on $\mathcal R_\circ$ as in Lemma 3.6.

Proof. Lemma 3.6 supplies both geometric shape inverses, with unary sockets
unchanged. Lemma 6.5 supplies their basic extraction and exact replay, and
the memory decoder's extraction/reselection. For T, the first record has
the foundation as actual prestate; Lemma 5.4 gives the next native event,
constructor names and carrier. Repeating proves that each field-9 event
